      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-242818",
      ":question/problem": "Consider a circle $C_{1}$ of radius $5$ centered at $A(-1, 7)$ and a circle $C_{2}$ of radius $2$ centered at $B(4,-2)$. Prove that $C_{1}$ and $C_{2}$ are similar.\n\nLet $U$ be the unit circle centered at the origin.\n\nFirst, we will show that\n$C_{1}\u223cU$.\nFor the circle $C_{1}$ of radius $5$ centered at $A(-1, 7)$, applying a translation of\n{{field-1}}\nand\n{{field-2}}\nfollowed by a dilation of {{field-3}}\nmaps $C_{1}$ onto $U$."
